    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nOccupying an enviable position in one of South County Dublin's most prestigious coastal addresses, 28 Sandycove Avenue West is an exceptionally attractive end-of-terrace Victorian residence, effortlessly combining timeless period elegance with the unrivalled lifestyle that has made Sandycove one of Dublin's most coveted locations.\n\nExtending to approximately 128 sq.m (1,375 sq.ft.), this beautifully proportioned home offers bright, spacious accommodation throughout, complemented by a highly desirable sunny west-facing rear garden—an ideal setting for outdoor entertaining or quiet relaxation in the afternoon and evening sunshine.\n\nJust moments from the shoreline, the property enjoys immediate access to the iconic Sandycove Harbour and the celebrated Forty Foot, where generations have embraced the tradition of year-round sea swimming. This exceptional setting offers a unique blend of coastal tranquillity and vibrant village living, creating an outstanding lifestyle opportunity for discerning purchasers.\n\nThe surrounding area is renowned for its exceptional educational facilities, with many of Dublin's finest primary and secondary schools within easy reach, including Castle Park School, Harold National School, Rathdown School, Loreto Abbey Dalkey, Cluny School, and Holy Child Killiney.\n\nFor those with an active lifestyle, the choice of recreational amenities is second to none. Sandycove Tennis Club is just a short stroll away on Elton Park, while Cuala GAA Club and Dalkey United AFC are close at hand. Sailing enthusiasts will appreciate the proximity of the four prestigious yacht clubs surrounding Dún Laoghaire Harbour, together with its world-class marina and extensive waterfront facilities.\n\nPerfectly positioned between the charming villages of Glasthule and Dalkey, residents enjoy an outstanding selection of artisan cafés, award-winning restaurants, stylish boutiques, welcoming pubs and everyday conveniences, all within walking distance. Excellent public transport, including nearby DART stations and frequent bus services, provides swift and convenient access to Dublin City Centre and beyond.\n\nSteeped in history and culture, the area is home to many of Dublin's most treasured landmarks, including the historic Martello Tower at Sandycove Point, immortalised in James Joyce's Ulysses, the medieval Dalkey Castle, and the ever-popular People's Park, renowned for its vibrant Sunday Farmers' Market. Combined with the scenic promenades, picturesque coastline and the magnificent piers of Dún Laoghaire Harbour, the location offers an exceptional balance of heritage, natural beauty and modern convenience.\n\nRarely does a home become available that so perfectly encapsulates the charm of Victorian architecture, the appeal of coastal living and the convenience of one of Dublin's most desirable residential settings. 28 Sandycove Avenue West represents an outstanding opportunity to acquire a distinguished family home in a truly exceptional location."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPorched Entrance - 1.00m x 1.70m\n\n\nReception Hall - 5.95m x 1.70m\n\n\nSitting Room - 4.00m x 3.60m\n\n\nLiving Room - 7.05m x 3.90m\ndual aspect front to back\n\nBedroom 2 - \n\n\nUtility Room - 1.75m x 1.75m\n\n\nShower Room - \n\n\nKitchen/Breakfast Room - 3.70m x 3.75m\nopens out to the sunny west facing rear garden\n\nAtrium - 2.2m x 2.4m\nwith door to the garden and a spiral stairwell leading up to the sun room\n\nUpstairs - \nwith hot press\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.95m x 3.70m\nwith access to a mezzanine that looks down into the garden\n\nSunroom - 2.20m x 3.60m\n\n\nShower Room - \n\n\nSeparate W.C. - \n\n\nOutside - \nrear garden faces west with lovely granite walls, pond, mature planting, gate out to the lane, boiler house with gas fired heating and storage\n\n"
      },
      {
